{"schema": 1, "provider": "codex", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "request_sha256": "57d79559d3e1f622de0c831d633179cd9e56a68113c10f851861875a76aab5ae", "invocation_metadata": {"schema": 1, "image_id": "sha256:79462fb575e55c574c60e95256406443339fd0aebddbaddec572b8d1b632ae39", "executable_path": "/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js", "executable_sha256": "61b0194f3bb6534439c8d26a3ed57d0805f84b884588b761795323eeb92fcf70", "known_configuration_path": "/home/codex/.codex/config.toml", "known_configuration_sha256": "c8597a1fbc447e945c45fc00126a131d9c3a824d2e6f96a57288de382363b87a", "other_effective_configuration": "unknown; trusted launcher/profile boundary", "response_schema_sha256": "374d4bb692012196f95c8105308100b0aeebe7a8fcc28fcb12010183313548a8", "response_schema_scope": "Prompt guidance and strict local validation only; no provider enforcement claim", "public_model_catalog_sha256": "fd219bd9f061278275f528939f82f54d2eb97df4b25c23b022adbe48813d920b", "runtime_model_catalog_sha256": "5f16461bf0477c6e522b6cdbb66d627a246e0da675721fe8cb8b35163cb736c9", "tool_surface_override": "direct; no shell, patch, search or experimental tools", "requested_reasoning_effort": "medium", "effective_remote_reasoning_effort": "not observed", "effective_features": {"disabled_features": ["apps", "plugins", "remote_plugin", "hooks", "daemon_auto_start", "shell_tool", "code_mode_host", "browser_use", "browser_use_external", "browser_use_full_cdp_access", "computer_use", "in_app_browser", "image_generation", "view_image", "multi_agent", "multi_agent_v2", "skill_search", "sleep_tool", "goals", "tool_suggest", "workspace_dependencies", "request_permissions_tool", "agent_message_board"], "unified_exec_observed": true, "shell_registration_control": "shell_tool=false; Codex 0.160.0 spec_plan.rs", "complete_configuration_isolation": false}}, "native_exit_code": 0, "usage_reported": {"input_tokens": 25549, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_write_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 6218, "reasoning_output_tokens": 516}, "native_reconnections": [], "result": {"schema": 1, "reason": "Se aporta únicamente una batería nueva y su trazabilidad, sin modificar topo_plan.py ni README.md. Cubre criterios originales, oráculo independiente, límites, errores y atomicidad. No se ha ejecutado ni se afirma ningún resultado.", "files": {"test_topo_plan.py": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline contract tests. Run with the fixed host argv; no installation needed.\"\"\"\nimport contextlib\nimport copy\nimport io\nimport itertools\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport random\nimport runpy\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport unittest\n\nPROGRAM = Path(__file__).resolve().with_name('topo_plan.py')\nLIMIT = 131072\nERROR = b'topo-plan: invalid input\\n'\nEMPTY = {'nodes': [], 'edges': []}\n\n\ndef encode(request):\n    return json.dumps(request, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(',', ':')).encode('ascii')\n\n\ndef oracle(request):\n    \"\"\"Inspect remaining predecessors directly; no indegrees or heap.\"\"\"\n    nodes = set(request['nodes'])\n    predecessors = {n: set() for n in nodes}\n    for source, target in request['edges']:\n        predecessors[target].add(source)\n    remaining = set(nodes)\n    order = []\n    while remaining:\n        available = [n for n in remaining if not (predecessors[n] & remaining)]\n        if not available:\n            raise ValueError('cycle')\n        node = min(available)\n        order.append(node)\n        remaining.remove(node)\n    remaining = set(nodes)\n    layers = []\n    while remaining:\n        frontier = sorted(n for n in remaining if not (predecessors[n] & remaining))\n        if not frontier:\n            raise ValueError('cycle')\n        layers.append(frontier)\n        remaining.difference_update(frontier)\n    return {'order': order, 'layers': layers, 'roots': layers[0][:] if layers else []}\n\n\nclass NoRead:\n    @property\n    def buffer(self):\n        return self\n\n    def read(self, *args):\n        raise AssertionError('import read stdin')\n\n\nclass ShortReader:\n    def __init__(self, data, width):\n        self.data = data\n        self.width = width\n        self.position = 0\n        self.requests = []\n\n    def read(self, size):\n        self.requests.append(size)\n        end = min(len(self.data), self.position + min(size, self.width))\n        chunk = self.data[self.position:end]\n        self.position = end\n        return chunk\n\n\nclass TopoPlanTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        # Absolute runpy loading under -I; imports must not activate the CLI.\n        out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n        original_stdin = sys.stdin\n        try:\n            sys.stdin = NoRead()\n            with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n                cls.module = runpy.run_path(str(PROGRAM), run_name='topo_plan_contract_tests')\n        finally:\n            sys.stdin = original_stdin\n        if out.getvalue() or err.getvalue():\n            raise AssertionError('import emitted output')\n\n    def invoke(self, data):\n        # runpy explicitly loads the sealed program by absolute path in every CLI run.\n        script = 'import runpy; runpy.run_path(' + repr(str(PROGRAM)) + ', run_name=\"__main__\")'\n        return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-I', '-B', '-c', script],\n                              input=data, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n                              timeout=5, check=False)\n\n    def valid(self, data, expected):\n        result = self.invoke(data)\n        self.assertTrue(result.returncode == 0, 'valid batch exit code')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr == b'', 'valid batch stderr must be empty')\n        if not expected:\n            self.assertTrue(result.stdout == b'', 'zero requests must emit zero bytes')\n            return\n        self.assertTrue(result.stdout.endswith(b'\\n'), 'missing final newline')\n        lines = result.stdout[:-1].split(b'\\n')\n        self.assertTrue(len(lines) == len(expected), 'response count or framing differs')\n        def unique(pairs):\n            obj = {}\n            for key, value in pairs:\n                if key in obj:\n                    raise ValueError('duplicate output key')\n                obj[key] = value\n            return obj\n        def nonfinite(value):\n            raise ValueError('nonfinite output')\n        for index, (line, wanted) in enumerate(zip(lines, expected)):\n            actual = json.loads(line.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique,\n                                parse_constant=nonfinite)\n            self.assertTrue(isinstance(actual, dict), 'output must be an object')\n            self.assertTrue(set(actual) == {'order', 'layers', 'roots'}, 'output keys differ')\n            self.assertTrue(actual == wanted, 'response mismatch at index %d' % index)\n\n    def invalid(self, data):\n        result = self.invoke(data)\n        self.assertTrue(result.returncode == 2, 'invalid input must exit 2')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stdout == b'', 'invalid batch emitted a partial response')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr == ERROR, 'invalid input diagnostic differs')\n\n    def valid_requests(self, requests):\n        self.valid(b'\\n'.join(encode(r) for r in requests) + b'\\n',\n                   [oracle(r) for r in requests])\n\n    def test_public_examples_and_structural_cases(self):\n        examples = [\n            ({'nodes': ['z', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]},\n             {'order': ['a', 'b', 'z'], 'layers': [['a', 'z'], ['b']], 'roots': ['a', 'z']}),\n            ({'nodes': ['c', 'a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'c'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'c']]},\n             {'order': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'layers': [['a', 'b'], ['c']], 'roots': ['a', 'b']}),\n            (EMPTY, {'order': [], 'layers': [], 'roots': []})]\n        self.valid(b'\\n'.join(encode(r) for r, _ in examples) + b'\\n',\n                   [expected for _, expected in examples])\n        self.valid_requests([\n            {'nodes': ['a'], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'a', 'aa', 'a0', 'a_'], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': ['d', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd']]},\n            {'nodes': ['e', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'],\n             'edges': [['a', 'c'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd'], ['c', 'e']]},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'y', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['y', 'z']]},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'],\n             'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]}\n        ])\n\n    def test_exhaustive_small_graphs(self):\n        names = ['a', 'b', 'c']\n        candidates = [(a, b) for a in names for b in names if a != b]\n        valid = []\n        for mask in range(1 << len(candidates)):\n            request = {'nodes': names[::-1],\n                       'edges': [list(edge) for i, edge in enumerate(candidates) if mask & (1 << i)]}\n            try:\n                oracle(request)\n            except ValueError:\n                with self.subTest(cyclic_mask=mask):\n                    self.invalid(encode(request))\n            else:\n                valid.append(request)\n        self.valid_requests(valid)\n        # All forward-edge subsets under every ordering of four nodes.\n        # This visits every labelled four-node DAG, possibly more than once.\n        batch = []\n        for permutation in itertools.permutations(['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']):\n            edges = list(itertools.combinations(permutation, 2))\n            for mask in range(64):\n                batch.append({'nodes': list(reversed(permutation)),\n                              'edges': [list(e) for i, e in enumerate(edges) if mask & (1 << i)]})\n                if len(batch) == 80:\n                    self.valid_requests(batch)\n                    batch = []\n        if batch:\n            self.valid_requests(batch)\n\n    def test_deterministic_variations_and_generated_dags(self):\n        rng = random.Random(18473)\n        requests = []\n        for size in range(1, 13):\n            for _ in range(5):\n                names = ['n%02d' % i for i in range(size)]\n                rng.shuffle(names)\n                edges = [list(e) for e in itertools.combinations(names, 2) if rng.random() < 0.3]\n                base = {'nodes': names[:], 'edges': edges}\n                expected = oracle(base)\n                for variation in range(3):\n                    changed = copy.deepcopy(base)\n                    rng.shuffle(changed['nodes'])\n                    if changed['edges']:\n                        changed['edges'] += copy.deepcopy(changed['edges'][:variation + 1])\n                    rng.shuffle(changed['edges'])\n                    self.assertTrue(oracle(changed) == expected, 'fixture variation changed graph')\n                    requests.append(changed)\n        for start in range(0, len(requests), 40):\n            self.valid_requests(requests[start:start + 40])\n\n    def test_internal_graph_state_independence(self):\n        # Supplement external behavior with the original C09 state invariant.\n        request = {'nodes': ['z', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'],\n                   'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]}\n        original = copy.deepcopy(request)\n        adjacency, indegree = self.module['normalize_graph'](request)\n        saved = copy.deepcopy((adjacency, indegree))\n        expected = oracle(request)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            for function, key in [('topological_order', 'order'), ('topological_layers', 'layers'),\n                                  ('topological_layers', 'layers'), ('topological_order', 'order')]:\n                actual = self.module[function](adjacency, indegree)\n                self.assertTrue(actual == expected[key], 'repeated planning differs')\n                self.assertTrue((adjacency, indegree) == saved, 'planner mutated graph base')\n            self.assertTrue(self.module['plan_request'](request) == expected, 'plan_request differs')\n            self.assertTrue(request == original, 'request object mutated')\n\n    def test_schema_names_and_edge_types(self):\n        cases = []\n        for top in [None, True, 1, 'x', [], [EMPTY]]:\n            cases.append(top)\n        cases += [{}, {'nodes': []}, {'edges': []},\n                  {'nodes': [], 'edges': [], 'extra': 0}]\n        for value in [None, True, 3, 'a', {}, {'a': 1}]:\n            cases += [{'nodes': value, 'edges': []}, {'nodes': [], 'edges': value}]\n        for name in ['', 'A', '0a', '_a', 'a-b', 'a.b', 'a b', 'a\\n', 'a\\r', 'a\\x00',\n                     'é', 'ａ', 'a' * 17, None, True, 2, [], {}]:\n            cases.append({'nodes': [name], 'edges': []})\n        cases.append({'nodes': ['a', 'a'], 'edges': []})\n        for edge in [None, True, 1, 'ab', {}, [], ['a'], ['a', 'b', 'a']]:\n            cases.append({'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [edge]})\n        for endpoint in [None, False, 0, [], {}, 'unknown', 'A']:\n            cases += [{'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [[endpoint, 'b']]},\n                      {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', endpoint]]}]\n        cases += [{'nodes': ['a'], 'edges': [['a', 'a']]},\n                  {'nodes': [], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}]\n        for index, request in enumerate(cases):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(encode(request))\n        self.valid(b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\u0061\",\"a0\",\"a_\",\"a123456789012345\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   [oracle({'nodes': ['a', 'a0', 'a_', 'a123456789012345'], 'edges': []})])\n        escaped = b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\\\u0061\",\"b\"],\"edges\":[[\"\\\\u0061\",\"b\"]]}'\n        self.valid(escaped, [{'order': ['a', 'b'], 'layers': [['a'], ['b']], 'roots': ['a']}])\n\n    def test_strict_json_and_transport(self):\n        base = encode(EMPTY)\n        invalid = [b'\\n', b' ', b'\\t\\r\\n', base + b'\\n\\n',\n                   base + b'\\n\\n' + base, b'\\n' + base,\n                   b'{', base[:-1], base + b' garbage', base + base,\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[],\\n\"edges\":[]}', base + b'\\r' + base,\n                   b'\\xef\\xbb\\xbf' + base, b'\\xff', base + b'\\n\\xff',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\xc0\\xaf\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\xed\\xa0\\x80\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[],\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[{\"x\":1,\"x\":2}],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[{\"x\":1,\"x\":2}]}',\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],}',\n                   b\"{'nodes':[],'edges':[]}\",\n                   b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\\\ud800\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n                   base + '\\u2028'.encode('utf-8') + base,\n                   base + b'\\x0b' + base]\n        for token in [b'NaN', b'Infinity', b'-Infinity']:\n            invalid += [token, b'{\"nodes\":' + token + b',\"edges\":[]}',\n                        b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"extra\":' + token + b'}']\n        invalid += [b'{\"nodes\":[' + b'[' * 1500 + b'0' + b']' * 1500 + b'],\"edges\":[]}',\n                    b'{\"nodes\":[' + b'9' * 10000 + b'],\"edges\":[]}',\n                    b'{\"nodes\":[1e9999],\"edges\":[]}']\n        for index, data in enumerate(invalid):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(data)\n        expected = oracle(EMPTY)\n        for data in [base, base + b'\\n', base + b'\\r\\n', b' \\t' + base + b' \\r',\n                     base + b'\\r']:\n            with self.subTest(valid_transport=data[:4]):\n                self.valid(data, [expected])\n        self.valid(b'', [])\n        second = {'nodes': ['b', 'a'], 'edges': []}\n        self.valid(base + b'\\r\\n' + encode(second), [expected, oracle(second)])\n\n    def test_inclusive_limits(self):\n        names = ['n%03d' % i for i in range(120)]\n        self.valid_requests([{'nodes': names[::-1], 'edges': []},\n                             {'nodes': names, 'edges': [[names[i], names[i + 1]] for i in range(119)]},\n                             {'nodes': ['a' * 16], 'edges': []},\n                             {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']] * 2000}])\n        for request in [{'nodes': names + ['n120'], 'edges': []},\n                        {'nodes': ['a' * 17], 'edges': []},\n                        {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']] * 2001}]:\n            self.invalid(encode(request))\n        # Exactly 2000 distinct edges, as well as the duplicate-edge boundary above.\n        candidates = [list(e) for e in itertools.combinations(names, 2)]\n        self.valid_requests([{'nodes': names, 'edges': candidates[:2000]}])\n        self.invalid(encode({'nodes': names, 'edges': candidates[:2001]}))\n        base = encode(EMPTY)\n        exact = base + b' ' * (LIMIT - len(base) - 1) + b'\\n'\n        self.assertTrue(len(exact) == LIMIT, 'incorrect byte-limit fixture')\n        self.valid(exact, [oracle(EMPTY)])\n        self.invalid(exact + b' ')\n        self.valid(base + b' ' * (LIMIT - len(base)), [oracle(EMPTY)])\n        self.invalid(base + b' ' * (LIMIT + 1 - len(base)))\n        prefix = base + b'\\n'\n        tail = base + b' ' * (LIMIT - len(prefix) - len(base))\n        self.valid(prefix + tail, [oracle(EMPTY), oracle(EMPTY)])\n        self.invalid(prefix + tail + b' ')\n\n    def test_bounded_reader_with_short_reads(self):\n        reader = self.module['read_bounded']\n        for data, width in [(b'', 1), (encode(EMPTY), 1), (b'x' * LIMIT, 997)]:\n            stream = ShortReader(data, width)\n            actual = reader(stream)\n            self.assertTrue(actual == data, 'short read lost bytes')\n            self.assertTrue(all(0 < n <= LIMIT + 1 for n in stream.requests), 'unbounded read request')\n        stream = ShortReader(b'x' * (LIMIT + 20), 997)\n        with self.assertRaises(self.module['InvalidInput']):\n            reader(stream)\n        self.assertTrue(stream.position == LIMIT + 1, 'reader consumed beyond sentinel byte')\n        self.assertTrue(all(0 < n <= LIMIT + 1 for n in stream.requests), 'unbounded read request')\n\n    def test_cycles_and_batch_atomicity(self):\n        cycles = [\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'a']]},\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'],\n             'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd'], ['d', 'a']]},\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b', 'x', 'y', 'z'],\n             'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['x', 'y'], ['y', 'z'], ['z', 'x']]}\n        ]\n        prefix = encode({'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}) + b'\\n'\n        suffix = encode(EMPTY) + b'\\n'\n        bad_lines = [encode(r) for r in cycles] + [b'{', b'\\xff', b'',\n                     b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"extra\":0}',\n                     b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"nodes\":[]}']\n        for index, bad in enumerate(bad_lines):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(prefix + bad + b'\\n')\n                self.invalid(bad + b'\\n' + suffix)\n                self.invalid(prefix * 40 + bad + b'\\n' + suffix)\n        self.valid_requests([EMPTY, {'nodes': ['b', 'a'], 'edges': []}, EMPTY,\n                             {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Fail-fast bounds ordinary diagnostic volume without truncating reports.\n    unittest.main(verbosity=1, failfast=True)\n", "TEST_BATTERY.md": "# Batería separada de TopoPlan\n\nEsta entrega añade test_topo_plan.py y este documento. No reemplaza programa, README, criterios originales ni capturas históricas. No contiene resultados de ejecución, recibos, aprobación ni auditoría.\n\nComando fijo suministrado:\n\n    /opt/specorganon/venv/bin/python -I -B /input/delivery/test_topo_plan.py\n\nLa batería usa unittest y otras bibliotecas estándar. Resuelve topo_plan.py junto al archivo de pruebas por ruta absoluta y lo carga con runpy, sin modificar sys.path. Cada ejecución de CLI también utiliza runpy con esa ruta absoluta, en un proceso Python aislado con -I y -B. No necesita instalación, red, fixtures externos ni archivos temporales. Los fixtures están incorporados en el archivo nuevo.\n\nCorrespondencia con criterios originales:\n\n- C01–C03 / V04–V05: cero bytes, transporte LF/CRLF, última línea sin terminador, whitespace, líneas vacías, tamaño inclusivo y exceso, UTF-8 inválido, BOM, JSON inválido, claves duplicadas, constantes no finitas, profundidad y números enormes.\n- C04–C05 / V03–V04: tipos de listas, nombres y extremos, patrón ASCII, escapes, duplicados de nodos, pares incorrectos, nombres desconocidos, bucles, 120/121 nodos, 16/17 caracteres y 2000/2001 aristas antes de deduplicar. Incluye el límite de aristas distintas y duplicadas.\n- C06–C10 / V01–V02: ejemplos públicos con expectativas explícitas, cadenas, aislados, convergencias, componentes separados, elección lexicográfica global, rondas completas, raíces y esquema exacto de salida. Un oráculo independiente examina directamente los predecesores que permanecen, sin heap ni grados incrementales. Se enumeran todos los grafos dirigidos sin bucles de tres nodos y todos los subconjuntos de aristas hacia adelante bajo cada permutación de cuatro nodos. También se incluyen DAG generados con semilla fija y variaciones de orden y duplicados.\n- C09 / V02: comprobación adicional de las funciones suministradas normalize_graph, topological_order, topological_layers y plan_request; repetición en ambos órdenes, conservación de adyacencia, grados y petición original.\n- C06 y C11 / V06: ciclos conectados y desconectados, errores iniciales y tardíos, prefijos válidos largos y exceso global de bytes. Cada rechazo verifica conjuntamente exit 2, stdout vacío y diagnóstico exacto.\n- C10–C12 / V07: importación sin lectura de stdin ni emisión, lotes ordenados, JSON estricto de salida, newline final, stderr y códigos de salida. La adquisición acotada recibe además fixtures de lecturas cortas y verifica el byte centinela. La batería no acredita por sí sola ausencia universal de acceso externo, compatibilidad con todas las versiones de Python ni cumplimiento documental o procedural completo.\n\nCada proceso tiene un timeout de cinco segundos. unittest se configura con failfast y mensajes breves, sin volcar entradas de 131072 bytes ni truncar diagnósticos. No se declara aquí que la batería cumpla una cuota de ejecución medida; el host conserva la medición y los streams reales.\n\nObservación documental sobre el texto suministrado: README dice «25 bytes» para el diagnóstico, pero el literal ASCII topo-plan: invalid input seguido de LF tiene 24 bytes. Las pruebas utilizan el literal contractual exacto. README permanece intacto; cualquier corrección corresponde al presupuesto posterior de reparación compartido.\n"}, "documents": {}}}
